Method toArray() returns `Object[]`. It returns `toArray(Object[].class);` which presumably returns an array of size equal to size().

We need to write an assert statement that expresses that the length of the returned array equals the number of elements in the deque.

We can refer to the returned array as `\result`. So length is `\result.length`. Number of elements is `this.size()`.

Thus assert: `assert \result.length == this.size();`

